1
00:00:04,335 --> 00:00:05,875
The one who almost died that day...

2
00:00:07,905 --> 00:00:09,075
wasn't me.

3
00:00:10,615 --> 00:00:11,775
The one who got stabbed...

4
00:00:16,415 --> 00:00:17,415
was you.

5
00:00:19,255 --> 00:00:21,325
What are you talking about? I have to work. Get out.

6
00:00:24,025 --> 00:00:25,155
No, Mi Young, wait.

7
00:00:25,395 --> 00:00:26,595
No, wait...

8
00:00:41,845 --> 00:00:42,915
It wasn't you.

9
00:00:45,075 --> 00:00:46,085
It was me.

10
00:00:47,745 --> 00:00:48,755
I...

11
00:00:51,655 --> 00:00:53,825
was the one who put you in danger.

12
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,555
I...

13
00:00:57,525 --> 00:00:59,565
I almost killed you.

14
00:01:01,725 --> 00:01:03,835
I'm sorry.

15
00:01:04,795 --> 00:01:05,805
I'm sorry.

16
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:08,105
I'm sorry.

17
00:01:11,175 --> 00:01:12,305
What do I...

18
00:01:14,845 --> 00:01:16,015
What do I do?

19
00:01:22,715 --> 00:01:23,755
Someone might see us.

20
00:01:24,285 --> 00:01:25,285
Get up.

21
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:36,395
Let's go.

22
00:01:36,965 --> 00:01:38,295
People are waiting.

23
00:01:52,115 --> 00:01:54,315
(Senior Vow Renewal Event)

24
00:02:08,325 --> 00:02:11,495
Okay, everyone, on the count of three,

25
00:02:11,935 --> 00:02:13,765
say "cheese."

26
00:02:15,775 --> 00:02:17,575
One, two.

27
00:02:19,745 --> 00:02:22,175
Oh? CEO Baek.

28
00:02:23,975 --> 00:02:24,975
Are you okay?

29
00:02:25,845 --> 00:02:26,845
I'm fine.

30
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:30,915
It looks like CEO Baek is moved.

31
00:02:31,085 --> 00:02:34,755
- You're making me teary-eyed. - Thank you, CEO Baek.

32
00:02:34,825 --> 00:02:36,525
- Please don't cry. - Don't cry.

33
00:02:36,525 --> 00:02:38,525
I'm sorry.

34
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:44,235
All right, let's take it again.

35
00:02:46,265 --> 00:02:48,265
One, two, three.

36
00:02:48,705 --> 00:02:50,875
Cheese.

37
00:02:58,475 --> 00:02:59,685
Good job, everyone.

38
00:03:00,345 --> 00:03:01,745
- Good work. - Thank you.

39
00:03:01,985 --> 00:03:02,985
Vice President Kang.

40
00:03:03,885 --> 00:03:05,825
Did CEO Ji already leave for the day?

41
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:07,425
He said he was tired and left early.

42
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:09,355
That makes sense.

43
00:03:09,695 --> 00:03:12,025
He didn't have a moment's rest all day.

44
00:03:12,695 --> 00:03:13,795
What about CEO Baek?

45
00:03:14,325 --> 00:03:15,865
CEO Baek is still in her office.

46
00:03:16,335 --> 00:03:17,335
She said she still has work to finish.

47
00:03:17,895 --> 00:03:21,605
On a day like this, we should be throwing a huge company party.

48
00:03:23,405 --> 00:03:25,945
I seriously need to find a new job.

49
00:03:26,745 --> 00:03:27,905
Darn it.

50
00:03:28,175 --> 00:03:30,045
Darn it, this is no fun at all.

51
00:03:32,715 --> 00:03:34,745
Hey, Manager Song, wait up.

52
00:03:45,665 --> 00:03:47,365
I want to die.

53
00:03:47,595 --> 00:03:48,865
I said don't.

54
00:04:12,185 --> 00:04:13,325
No, Mi Young, wait.

55
00:04:13,325 --> 00:04:14,485
No, wait.

56
00:04:14,485 --> 00:04:16,095
Mi Young, just wait.

57
00:05:07,945 --> 00:05:09,545
What are you doing here?

58
00:05:11,245 --> 00:05:12,945
Don't tell me you left your house again.

59
00:05:13,745 --> 00:05:15,415
Have a drink with me.

60
00:05:20,285 --> 00:05:23,055
I don't normally drink during work hours,

61
00:05:24,695 --> 00:05:26,325
but let's just say we're off the clock today.

62
00:05:29,695 --> 00:05:31,265
Thank you, Lawyer Jeon.

63
00:05:32,965 --> 00:05:34,335
Since we're off the clock,

64
00:05:35,005 --> 00:05:37,475
let's drop the formalities too.

65
00:05:38,845 --> 00:05:39,845
Cheers.

66
00:05:48,915 --> 00:05:49,955
The ratio is killer, isn't it?

67
00:05:50,685 --> 00:05:51,685
Yes.

68
00:05:52,115 --> 00:05:54,855
I'm practically a national champion when it comes to making somaek.

69
00:05:55,455 --> 00:05:58,055
Even somaek needs that sentimental touch in its ratio.

70
00:06:07,005 --> 00:06:08,005
So...

71
00:06:09,735 --> 00:06:11,705
are you ready to tell me now...

72
00:06:13,575 --> 00:06:15,275
about what happened today?

73
00:06:18,845 --> 00:06:19,845
Today...

74
00:06:23,455 --> 00:06:25,625
I found out something shocking.

75
00:06:28,185 --> 00:06:29,195
I...

76
00:06:34,825 --> 00:06:36,565
stabbed my husband.

77
00:06:38,195 --> 00:06:39,205
You stabbed him?

78
00:06:41,835 --> 00:06:42,905
Three years ago,

79
00:06:43,435 --> 00:06:46,975
I told you that my husband had assaulted me.

80
00:06:50,175 --> 00:06:51,175
Well...

81
00:06:53,715 --> 00:06:55,545
That wasn't true.

82
00:06:58,685 --> 00:06:59,685
That day,

83
00:07:01,625 --> 00:07:04,325
I was the one who hurt my husband.

84
00:07:08,725 --> 00:07:11,835
My husband didn't abandon me and run away.

85
00:07:15,105 --> 00:07:18,575
He ran out to save his own life.

86
00:07:27,515 --> 00:07:29,415
I completely lost it that day.

87
00:07:32,985 --> 00:07:34,025
I stabbed...

88
00:07:38,025 --> 00:07:39,425
my husband with a knife.

89
00:07:44,365 --> 00:07:46,365
He was the one who got hurt.

90
00:07:49,235 --> 00:07:52,275
How must he have felt being blamed all this time?

91
00:07:54,275 --> 00:07:55,745
And why did he...

92
00:07:58,515 --> 00:08:00,145
keep taking it all...

93
00:08:01,085 --> 00:08:03,155
and hiding the truth until now?

94
00:08:05,385 --> 00:08:06,385
And...

95
00:08:09,055 --> 00:08:10,055
why did I think...

96
00:08:11,025 --> 00:08:13,565
I knew everything about my husband?

97
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:17,065
Maybe that's why...

98
00:08:19,035 --> 00:08:20,665
you've ended up here.

99
00:08:24,735 --> 00:08:28,545
Then, starting now, let's use the lawsuit...

100
00:08:29,745 --> 00:08:31,245
to get to know him properly, one thing at a time.

101
00:08:33,285 --> 00:08:35,685
Whether our goal becomes an amicable divorce...

102
00:08:36,855 --> 00:08:38,755
or a dramatic reconciliation...

103
00:08:40,255 --> 00:08:42,595
is something we can decide after you truly get to know...

104
00:08:42,595 --> 00:08:43,725
your husband.

105
00:09:01,045 --> 00:09:02,045
Seung Ho.

106
00:09:03,315 --> 00:09:05,685
Are you hiding anything from me?

107
00:09:06,385 --> 00:09:08,515
What? What's this all of a sudden?

108
00:09:08,945 --> 00:09:10,585
Oh, come on, you know.

109
00:09:10,715 --> 00:09:13,055
Something you can't easily open up about,

110
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:16,525
even with family.

111
00:09:17,525 --> 00:09:18,855
A secret shame of your own?

112
00:09:19,865 --> 00:09:20,865
I don't know.

113
00:09:22,795 --> 00:09:25,335
- Crypto? - Gosh, forget it.

114
00:09:26,235 --> 00:09:27,835
Why? Did your wife find out?

115
00:09:28,335 --> 00:09:29,405
Is that why you came running here?

116
00:09:31,435 --> 00:09:35,305
I guess there are no real secrets in this world.

117
00:09:36,315 --> 00:09:38,015
Why did we have to run into each other then?

118
00:09:39,115 --> 00:09:40,585
In times like that, you just pretend you don't know.

119
00:09:43,255 --> 00:09:44,285
Pretend I don't know?

120
00:09:44,715 --> 00:09:46,285
The thing about life is...

121
00:09:46,955 --> 00:09:48,925
if you keep pretending you don't know and ignore it,

122
00:09:49,325 --> 00:09:50,995
it will eventually become insignificant.

123
00:09:52,055 --> 00:09:53,725
If you go on with life and completely ignore it,

124
00:09:54,265 --> 00:09:56,495
you'll just think, "Oh, right. That happened."

125
00:09:57,435 --> 00:09:58,835
"That time with crypto,"

126
00:10:00,535 --> 00:10:02,605
"I lost all my money."

127
00:10:03,535 --> 00:10:04,875
It's that kind of moment...

128
00:10:06,045 --> 00:10:07,805
of enlightenment that they say will come.

129
00:10:32,605 --> 00:10:33,665
Won Ho, you're back?

130
00:10:36,605 --> 00:10:38,405
- Yes. - Hey,

131
00:10:39,575 --> 00:10:40,645
would you like some black tea?

132
00:10:56,425 --> 00:10:57,455
Try it.

133
00:10:58,055 --> 00:10:59,095
It smells wonderful.

134
00:11:15,775 --> 00:11:17,645
I have something to tell you.

135
00:11:18,815 --> 00:11:20,385
Okay, go ahead.

136
00:11:22,215 --> 00:11:24,555
Can you just pretend you don't know?

137
00:11:26,225 --> 00:11:27,225
What?

138
00:11:28,955 --> 00:11:31,525
What you heard from Father Kwon today and...

139
00:11:32,325 --> 00:11:33,965
everything you saw today.

140
00:11:37,495 --> 00:11:39,765
Just pretend you didn't see or hear any of it.

141
00:11:42,235 --> 00:11:45,205
Why should I do that?

142
00:11:46,105 --> 00:11:48,175
Because it's been a long time.

143
00:11:52,985 --> 00:11:54,785
It really doesn't bother me anymore.

144
00:11:54,885 --> 00:11:57,855
I'm fine, so you don't have to worry about it.

145
00:12:00,285 --> 00:12:01,285
All right.

146
00:12:01,925 --> 00:12:04,225
Then I will.

147
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:07,225
Okay.

148
00:12:29,145 --> 00:12:30,285
(Father Kwon)

149
00:12:31,855 --> 00:12:32,855
Yes, Father.

150
00:12:32,925 --> 00:12:34,555
I'm surprised to get a call from you.

151
00:12:36,555 --> 00:12:37,555
Pardon?

152
00:12:39,395 --> 00:12:42,325
The vow renewal volunteer service we talked about?

153
00:12:43,295 --> 00:12:44,365
The thing is,

154
00:12:44,665 --> 00:12:47,105
it's not really something I can decide on my own.

155
00:12:50,375 --> 00:12:51,375
Really?

156
00:12:52,805 --> 00:12:54,245
Did Mi Young really say that?

157
00:12:56,615 --> 00:12:58,375
Do you think this is natural?

158
00:12:59,045 --> 00:13:00,045
What is?

159
00:13:00,685 --> 00:13:02,085
You said it yourself yesterday...

160
00:13:02,145 --> 00:13:04,115
that doing volunteer work right now makes no sense.

161
00:13:04,315 --> 00:13:05,915
You even called me hopeless.

162
00:13:06,125 --> 00:13:07,485
And whenever Father Kwon is mentioned,

163
00:13:07,555 --> 00:13:08,685
you can't stand him.

164
00:13:08,755 --> 00:13:10,855
Now you suddenly decide overnight that you're going to do it?

165
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,525
And you even called him yourself?

166
00:13:13,895 --> 00:13:16,235
Well, why not?

167
00:13:16,935 --> 00:13:19,805
I thought about it, and it seems like a good cause.

168
00:13:20,065 --> 00:13:21,365
Let's just do it, honey.

169
00:13:21,835 --> 00:13:23,505
"Let's just do it, honey?"

170
00:13:23,935 --> 00:13:25,975
Why? You don't want to?

171
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:31,375
Look, we made an agreement yesterday, right?

172
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:33,585
To act like yesterday never happened.

173
00:13:33,885 --> 00:13:35,385
Yes, so?

174
00:13:36,015 --> 00:13:37,315
No, what I mean is...

175
00:13:39,115 --> 00:13:41,225
Try to be more natural!

176
00:13:41,285 --> 00:13:43,155
Why are you suddenly acting so unlike yourself?

177
00:13:45,655 --> 00:13:46,695
I'm warning you.

178
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:49,225
If you're unnatural, you get a yellow card.

179
00:13:52,835 --> 00:13:54,105
That face gets you two.

180
00:13:57,375 --> 00:13:58,435
Darn it.

181
00:13:59,975 --> 00:14:01,045
Honey.

182
00:14:04,875 --> 00:14:06,015
Darn it, that's hot.

183
00:14:06,285 --> 00:14:09,045
Oh my, are you okay? Did you burn yourself?

184
00:14:09,555 --> 00:14:13,255
- Be careful. Give it to me. - No, I'm fine.

185
00:14:23,735 --> 00:14:25,135
We have five design proposals...

186
00:14:25,135 --> 00:14:26,535
for the bride, Kim Jin Kyeong, right?

187
00:14:26,735 --> 00:14:29,135
- Which did we narrow it down to? - This one and these.

188
00:14:29,205 --> 00:14:31,005
- These three? - Yes.

189
00:14:42,145 --> 00:14:43,355
What were they?

190
00:14:46,325 --> 00:14:47,585
What's with you two?

191
00:14:50,155 --> 00:14:51,155
Your wife.

192
00:14:51,725 --> 00:14:53,125
Why is she suddenly acting like that toward you?

193
00:14:54,865 --> 00:14:57,465
Is that part of her lawsuit strategy?

194
00:14:58,865 --> 00:14:59,865
Lawsuit strategy?

195
00:15:00,005 --> 00:15:01,565
To make you so uncomfortable...

196
00:15:01,805 --> 00:15:03,375
that you'll just give her the divorce, or something?

197
00:15:04,535 --> 00:15:05,835
Hey, you felt it too, right?

198
00:15:06,075 --> 00:15:07,275
Even just watching from the sidelines,

199
00:15:07,345 --> 00:15:08,775
it's incredibly awkward, isn't it?

200
00:15:08,875 --> 00:15:10,415
It's more than just awkward.

201
00:15:10,475 --> 00:15:11,915
She's like a completely different person.

202
00:15:14,015 --> 00:15:16,285
At this point, shouldn't we do some digging on her?

203
00:15:16,955 --> 00:15:18,985
Like maybe she took out a loan against your house or something.

204
00:15:20,485 --> 00:15:21,755
No, it's not like that.

205
00:15:22,355 --> 00:15:23,395
Then what is it?

206
00:15:23,925 --> 00:15:25,995
There really is something going on between you two, isn't there?

207
00:15:27,425 --> 00:15:28,595
I don't know.

208
00:15:31,665 --> 00:15:34,005
This is really becoming a problem.

209
00:15:40,805 --> 00:15:43,115
I was so impressed.

210
00:15:43,575 --> 00:15:45,715
How can you be so nice to Won Ho?

211
00:15:47,885 --> 00:15:49,615
Did it look that way to you too?

212
00:15:49,855 --> 00:15:52,155
Yes. He might just pack his bags and leave.

213
00:15:54,325 --> 00:15:57,955
You're being so uncomfortably nice to him...

214
00:15:58,055 --> 00:16:00,025
to make Won Ho leave on his own accord,

215
00:16:00,725 --> 00:16:01,825
is that it?

216
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:04,035
Anyway, CEO Baek,

217
00:16:04,095 --> 00:16:05,965
you are so brilliant.

218
00:16:06,205 --> 00:16:09,405
How do I usually treat Ji Won Ho, then?

219
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,735
Are you kidding?

220
00:16:10,875 --> 00:16:12,775
You treated him worse than dirt.

221
00:16:12,905 --> 00:16:15,345
Sometimes you'd treat Won Ho like he was invisible,

222
00:16:15,405 --> 00:16:17,045
not speaking to him or answering him.

223
00:16:17,575 --> 00:16:19,175
Was I really that bad?

224
00:16:19,375 --> 00:16:22,715
The person involved is always the last to know.

225
00:16:23,215 --> 00:16:25,455
Anyway, just keep it up a little longer.

226
00:16:25,815 --> 00:16:28,855
I bet Won Ho will be out of the house before the weekend.

227
00:16:29,225 --> 00:16:30,555
I bet 50 cents on it.

228
00:16:34,195 --> 00:16:37,465
Excuse me, Young Min. Is the thing I asked for earlier ready?

229
00:16:51,875 --> 00:16:53,745
I figured you'd be here already.

230
00:16:54,385 --> 00:16:56,045
How did you know I was here?

231
00:16:56,215 --> 00:16:57,415
Are you spying on me?

232
00:16:57,485 --> 00:16:58,555
Am I allowed to?

233
00:16:59,625 --> 00:17:01,825
I'm not in the mood for jokes right now.

234
00:17:02,485 --> 00:17:05,495
Why? Is something wrong?

235
00:17:05,855 --> 00:17:07,665
It's none of your business.

236
00:17:08,395 --> 00:17:09,425
Come on.

237
00:17:09,965 --> 00:17:11,965
But I tell you everything about me.

238
00:17:12,235 --> 00:17:14,305
That's my point. Why would you trust me?

239
00:17:14,735 --> 00:17:16,065
If you keep trusting people that easily,

240
00:17:16,135 --> 00:17:17,305
you're going to ruin your life.

241
00:17:19,805 --> 00:17:23,845
If I'm going to ruin it, I want to ruin it with you.

242
00:17:25,845 --> 00:17:27,945
I told you not to cross the line, didn't I?

243
00:17:30,855 --> 00:17:32,185
Are you going home today?

244
00:17:33,485 --> 00:17:34,585
Why do you ask?

245
00:17:36,855 --> 00:17:38,995
Don't go home.

246
00:17:39,255 --> 00:17:43,365
Just hang out with me. Let's get hammered.

247
00:17:43,465 --> 00:17:45,295
No way. Who knows what trouble we'd get into.

248
00:17:45,495 --> 00:17:47,405
I'm never getting wasted with you again.

249
00:17:48,105 --> 00:17:49,105
What?

250
00:17:49,265 --> 00:17:51,135
You're not planning on going home today,

251
00:17:51,475 --> 00:17:52,475
right?

252
00:17:54,045 --> 00:17:55,075
Why don't you just...

253
00:17:55,375 --> 00:17:57,215
never go home again?

254
00:17:57,415 --> 00:17:59,685
Stop talking nonsense. Just drink up and go.

255
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,745
Darn it.

256
00:18:25,575 --> 00:18:27,805
I haven't had enough to drink yet.

257
00:18:29,045 --> 00:18:32,745
Can we go inside and have just one more drink?

258
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,645
There you go again, asking for trouble.

259
00:18:34,715 --> 00:18:36,955
Hurry and go. You'll miss the last bus.

260
00:18:37,385 --> 00:18:38,515
You really want me to go?

261
00:18:39,315 --> 00:18:40,385
Go, already.

262
00:18:40,655 --> 00:18:42,285
If you keep this up, I'll seriously...

263
00:18:42,425 --> 00:18:44,525
- Seriously. - won't hang out with you anymore.

264
00:18:46,925 --> 00:18:48,325
Look at that face.

265
00:18:49,095 --> 00:18:50,465
It's so cute.

266
00:18:51,765 --> 00:18:53,805
What? You always laugh at the weirdest things.

267
00:18:54,265 --> 00:18:55,305
Hurry up and go.

268
00:18:55,605 --> 00:18:56,605
Okay.

269
00:18:57,275 --> 00:18:58,275
Sleep well.

270
00:19:02,145 --> 00:19:04,145
(Jihwaja Motel)

271
00:19:04,915 --> 00:19:06,215
I told you to go.

272
00:19:06,445 --> 00:19:07,445
Okay.

273
00:19:25,135 --> 00:19:26,135
What the...

274
00:19:28,835 --> 00:19:31,235
Why do you keep coming here? Why aren't you sleeping at home?

275
00:19:31,905 --> 00:19:34,505
Let's go. Hurry. I made dinner at home.

276
00:19:35,175 --> 00:19:36,775
Seriously, what's going on?

277
00:19:37,575 --> 00:19:39,985
Since when have you ever worried about me like this?

278
00:19:40,545 --> 00:19:44,085
You don't care where I pass out or what I eat.

279
00:19:46,785 --> 00:19:49,185
Just act like you normally do, please.

280
00:19:50,195 --> 00:19:51,595
It's not like I'm asking you to be nice to me.

281
00:19:51,655 --> 00:19:55,225
Just go your way, and I'll go mine. Just let me live in peace.

282
00:19:55,295 --> 00:19:57,395
Why are you making such a fuss and bothering me?

283
00:19:58,465 --> 00:19:59,595
Won Ho.

284
00:19:59,595 --> 00:20:02,265
It's harder for me when you act like this.

285
00:20:04,705 --> 00:20:07,675
It makes me uncomfortable. It makes you uncomfortable too.

286
00:20:07,875 --> 00:20:08,875
It's just...

287
00:20:09,245 --> 00:20:11,915
Life becomes uncomfortable.

288
00:20:14,415 --> 00:20:16,145
So just leave me alone, will you?

289
00:20:19,155 --> 00:20:20,185
All right.

290
00:20:21,725 --> 00:20:22,855
I'll go then.

291
00:20:23,795 --> 00:20:24,795
But...

292
00:20:26,325 --> 00:20:27,325
I want you to know...

293
00:20:28,325 --> 00:20:30,935
it's not that I didn't ask because I didn't care.

294
00:20:32,395 --> 00:20:35,805
I may not have been nice to you or ever really showed it.

295
00:20:38,935 --> 00:20:40,645
But I was always worried.

296
00:20:42,945 --> 00:20:44,015
The truth is,

297
00:20:46,015 --> 00:20:48,515
I've always been concerned about you.

298
00:21:22,985 --> 00:21:24,015
Hello.

299
00:21:52,515 --> 00:21:55,385
(Jihwaja Motel)

300
00:22:27,245 --> 00:22:30,655
Mi Young. Did you see the supermoon tonight?

301
00:22:44,935 --> 00:22:46,165
To think...

302
00:22:46,435 --> 00:22:48,505
I'm drinking with you on the night of a supermoon.

303
00:22:49,305 --> 00:22:50,835
My prayers to the moon were answered.

304
00:22:53,645 --> 00:22:56,205
Thank you. If it wasn't for you,

305
00:22:56,945 --> 00:22:58,775
I wouldn't have even known there was a moon out.

306
00:23:01,185 --> 00:23:03,715
Are you really okay?

307
00:23:06,455 --> 00:23:08,685
You don't look well.

308
00:23:09,385 --> 00:23:11,855
Why? Do I look that bad?

309
00:23:12,625 --> 00:23:14,425
No, that's not what I meant.

310
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:23,835
I think my husband...

311
00:23:25,805 --> 00:23:27,575
is dating Hee Ju.

312
00:23:29,445 --> 00:23:30,445
What?

313
00:23:31,375 --> 00:23:34,485
I just went to the motel to get my husband,

314
00:23:35,685 --> 00:23:37,515
and Hee Ju was in the hallway.

315
00:23:39,555 --> 00:23:42,425
He blew up when he saw me,

316
00:23:44,355 --> 00:23:46,125
and I think it must have been because of Hee Ju.

317
00:23:57,535 --> 00:23:59,635
I thought I knew everything.

318
00:24:02,045 --> 00:24:04,115
I even thought I was okay with it.

319
00:24:09,215 --> 00:24:10,485
But now that it's actually happening,

320
00:24:11,515 --> 00:24:12,655
it feels strange.

321
00:24:16,825 --> 00:24:18,025
Hey, Mi Young.

322
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:21,125
If by any chance...

323
00:24:22,465 --> 00:24:25,035
- If you're having a hard time... - No.

324
00:24:25,465 --> 00:24:28,105
I'm not having a hard time. Let's just drink.

325
00:24:49,255 --> 00:24:50,755
You have to nip this in the bud.

326
00:24:51,195 --> 00:24:53,965
So you're saying he slept here last night too?

327
00:24:54,025 --> 00:24:56,065
Mi Young came to get him, but he still stayed the night.

328
00:24:56,125 --> 00:24:57,395
He sent her home alone.

329
00:24:57,465 --> 00:24:59,035
That mindless fool...

330
00:24:59,095 --> 00:25:00,605
Hey, pack up every single thing here,

331
00:25:00,605 --> 00:25:02,235
down to his last pair of underwear.

332
00:25:02,335 --> 00:25:04,775
Let's clean this whole place out so he can never come back.

333
00:25:04,775 --> 00:25:05,935
Yes, ma'am.

334
00:25:12,175 --> 00:25:14,815
- Wait. This isn't his. - What's with these clothes?

335
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:37,175
Just a second...

336
00:25:38,175 --> 00:25:39,935
Wait, hold on...

337
00:25:58,395 --> 00:25:59,495
(Open the door.)

338
00:26:10,175 --> 00:26:11,675
Hello? Is anyone here?

339
00:26:50,445 --> 00:26:51,945
She was very pretty.

340
00:27:27,885 --> 00:27:28,885
Oh my.

341
00:27:30,855 --> 00:27:33,055
- Who are you? - And who might you be,

342
00:27:33,115 --> 00:27:35,385
letting yourself into an empty house?

343
00:27:38,495 --> 00:27:39,495
Hey, Won Ho.

344
00:27:40,195 --> 00:27:41,195
What?

345
00:27:41,665 --> 00:27:43,995
Were you the one running... Oh, you are.

346
00:27:44,195 --> 00:27:46,865
Mom, she's the young woman I was telling you about,

347
00:27:47,005 --> 00:27:48,405
the one who came to the motel with Won Ho.

348
00:27:48,535 --> 00:27:49,635
What?

349
00:27:50,335 --> 00:27:51,405
Who are you?

350
00:27:51,875 --> 00:27:53,005
I'm...

351
00:27:53,675 --> 00:27:55,345
I'm CEO Ji's girlfriend.

352
00:27:55,805 --> 00:27:57,345
So you're saying that you're...

353
00:27:57,515 --> 00:28:00,245
my son, Ji Won Ho's, girlfriend?

354
00:28:01,715 --> 00:28:03,955
So you must be CEO Ji's mother.

355
00:28:04,255 --> 00:28:05,555
Hello. My name is...

356
00:28:05,615 --> 00:28:06,715
Ahn Hee Ju.

357
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:10,195
Hold on. You seem to be very confused.

358
00:28:10,455 --> 00:28:13,865
My son is already married.

359
00:28:13,865 --> 00:28:15,095
I know.

360
00:28:15,465 --> 00:28:18,095
- You know? - Yes. I'm well aware.

361
00:28:18,495 --> 00:28:21,505
Miss, I think it'd be best for you to leave now.

362
00:28:21,635 --> 00:28:23,205
You know he's married?

363
00:28:23,305 --> 00:28:25,805
Are you trying to break up a home?

364
00:28:26,075 --> 00:28:27,105
No way.

365
00:28:27,545 --> 00:28:29,945
CEO Ji's marriage fell apart ages ago.

366
00:28:30,515 --> 00:28:32,615
Don't tell me you didn't know.

367
00:28:32,815 --> 00:28:35,415
What? What did you just say?

368
00:28:35,485 --> 00:28:37,415
- What crap are you spouting now? - Mom, wait...

369
00:28:37,415 --> 00:28:38,485
You need to get out of here...

370
00:28:38,555 --> 00:28:39,555
- Let go of me. - Mom!

371
00:28:41,225 --> 00:28:42,255
Come here!

372
00:28:49,165 --> 00:28:50,595
I've thought about it,

373
00:28:51,465 --> 00:28:53,065
and rather than going on like this,

374
00:28:53,535 --> 00:28:55,435
I think it's best we end things quickly.

375
00:28:57,005 --> 00:28:59,805
We need to finalise the divorce...

376
00:28:59,805 --> 00:29:01,645
and sort out our lives.

377
00:29:01,645 --> 00:29:03,175
It will be a relief for everyone.

378
00:29:03,645 --> 00:29:05,045
Hee Ju included.

379
00:29:06,115 --> 00:29:07,115
Hee Ju?

380
00:29:08,015 --> 00:29:10,315
Hee Ju? Why are you bringing her up?

381
00:29:12,485 --> 00:29:13,855
Don't play dumb.

382
00:29:14,525 --> 00:29:16,855
I already know everything.

383
00:29:17,095 --> 00:29:19,555
That you two have been going in and out of motels.

384
00:29:19,855 --> 00:29:22,725
Oh, come on.

385
00:29:23,165 --> 00:29:25,365
I'm sick of making excuses.

386
00:29:25,435 --> 00:29:28,005
I told you it's not like that. It really isn't.

387
00:29:28,835 --> 00:29:32,205
And I know what you're misunderstanding about her,

388
00:29:32,275 --> 00:29:34,045
but it's because she's just different from others...

389
00:29:34,105 --> 00:29:35,105
How do I put this...

390
00:29:35,175 --> 00:29:37,215
She's special in her own way.

391
00:29:37,575 --> 00:29:39,815
What? Special?

392
00:29:40,075 --> 00:29:41,315
Yes.

393
00:29:44,185 --> 00:29:45,385
Why are you looking at me like that?

394
00:29:47,485 --> 00:29:48,725
- Let go of me! - Mom!

395
00:29:48,785 --> 00:29:50,755
- I said, let go. - Let go of me!

396
00:29:50,825 --> 00:29:52,225
- Let go of me! - Let go of her hair.

397
00:29:52,825 --> 00:29:55,865
- Let go. Miss. You let go first. - You let go first.

398
00:29:56,595 --> 00:29:58,435
- Mom. Stop it. - Why you...

399
00:29:58,435 --> 00:29:59,435
Let go!

400
00:30:02,205 --> 00:30:04,005
What? Girlfriend?

401
00:30:04,075 --> 00:30:05,635
Who is this crazy tramp?

402
00:30:05,705 --> 00:30:08,705
That's right, I'm his girlfriend!

403
00:30:08,705 --> 00:30:10,075
What did you say?

404
00:30:10,515 --> 00:30:11,515
That hurts!

405
00:30:12,315 --> 00:30:14,245
- That's nonsense! - I'm his girlfriend!

406
00:30:20,115 --> 00:30:21,625
Oh, my hair.

407
00:30:22,155 --> 00:30:23,455
Why you...

408
00:30:24,625 --> 00:30:27,165
How dare a brat like you act so bold?

409
00:30:27,925 --> 00:30:29,925
This lady is completely hopeless.

410
00:30:29,925 --> 00:30:32,195
- Do you have any idea who I am? - I don't, you tramp.

411
00:30:32,195 --> 00:30:34,005
Do I look like I need to know who you are?

412
00:30:34,105 --> 00:30:36,305
Where did Won Ho pick up such a leech?

413
00:30:36,365 --> 00:30:38,375
Both of you, just stop it. Come on, Mom.

414
00:30:38,575 --> 00:30:41,145
You. I'm not done with you.

415
00:30:41,605 --> 00:30:44,145
You're the one who's going to regret this.

416
00:30:45,445 --> 00:30:46,445
Hello?

417
00:30:46,815 --> 00:30:48,545
There's a crazy woman here. A psycho.

418
00:30:49,085 --> 00:30:50,385
Hello?

419
00:30:51,555 --> 00:30:53,785
So "special" people, when they drink and get sleepy,

420
00:30:53,925 --> 00:30:56,385
can just lie down and sleep wherever they want?

421
00:30:56,455 --> 00:30:59,625
Anyone can see she's not "special." She's weird.

422
00:30:59,725 --> 00:31:02,765
She's just weird and brazen. She's just too strange.

423
00:31:02,825 --> 00:31:05,035
I told you she's not. She's really a good person.

424
00:31:05,095 --> 00:31:07,805
She's just a little different from most people, that's all.

425
00:31:07,865 --> 00:31:09,365
What? A good person?

426
00:31:09,505 --> 00:31:10,535
What, special?

427
00:31:10,605 --> 00:31:11,605
Hey, you're unbelievable...

428
00:31:11,675 --> 00:31:13,475
No, when I said she's special, I meant...

429
00:31:13,535 --> 00:31:16,045
that she's just a bit different from other people her age.

430
00:31:16,045 --> 00:31:18,275
That's it. You'll see if you get to know her.

431
00:31:18,345 --> 00:31:20,815
I'm telling you, she's not like anyone else.

432
00:31:21,315 --> 00:31:23,245
You just won't give it up.

433
00:31:23,545 --> 00:31:24,555
What is wrong with you?

434
00:31:24,615 --> 00:31:26,115
How can you be so stubborn in the middle of all this?

435
00:31:26,255 --> 00:31:28,125
Hey, whether she's special or one of a kind,

436
00:31:28,185 --> 00:31:30,555
is that something you'd defend with your life?

437
00:31:30,625 --> 00:31:33,765
When did I ever say I'd defend her with my life?

438
00:31:33,895 --> 00:31:36,395
Then why do you keep nitpicking over something so small?

439
00:31:36,465 --> 00:31:37,565
What did I say about her?

440
00:31:37,635 --> 00:31:39,065
Did I call her pretty? What did I say?

441
00:31:39,135 --> 00:31:40,835
All I did was say one thing, that she was special,

442
00:31:40,905 --> 00:31:42,735
so why are you so fixated on it and making such a scene?

443
00:31:42,865 --> 00:31:45,705
Look at him, still insisting that she's special.

444
00:31:45,775 --> 00:31:47,105
Hey, nitpicking?

445
00:31:47,175 --> 00:31:50,005
- You're such a stubborn leech. - Yes, I'm a stubborn leech.

446
00:31:50,005 --> 00:31:51,515
But you're just pigheaded.

447
00:31:51,575 --> 00:31:53,445
Hey, you're the one who's stubborn for no reason, you jerk.

448
00:31:53,515 --> 00:31:54,645
Right back at you. Times a million.

449
00:31:54,715 --> 00:31:56,745
So childish. Unbelievably childish, really.

450
00:31:56,815 --> 00:31:58,285
You're the childish one.

451
00:31:58,355 --> 00:31:59,985
- Looks like they're finally... - You better watch your mouth!

452
00:31:59,985 --> 00:32:01,185
back to normal.

453
00:32:01,325 --> 00:32:05,325
It's awkward to watch, but why do I feel so relieved?

454
00:32:06,455 --> 00:32:08,495
I was so scared, my legs were shaking.

455
00:32:08,525 --> 00:32:10,495
- I'm so scared. - I'm not kidding.

456
00:32:10,495 --> 00:32:13,135
- Hey. Stop it. Okay? - Hey, Seung Ho.

457
00:32:16,265 --> 00:32:17,735
What? The police station?

458
00:32:19,805 --> 00:32:22,705
Wait, why Mi Young? Why does she have to come too?

459
00:32:25,515 --> 00:32:27,545
- Please calm down. - I'm so pissed off, darn it.

460
00:32:31,855 --> 00:32:33,415
This is my actual sister-in-law.

461
00:32:33,985 --> 00:32:35,025
This one is the fake one.

462
00:32:35,725 --> 00:32:37,025
Detective, if you were in her shoes,

463
00:32:37,195 --> 00:32:39,095
and a complete stranger popped out of your son's house...

464
00:32:39,225 --> 00:32:40,395
and pretended to be his wife,

465
00:32:40,465 --> 00:32:41,695
wouldn't you be shocked?

466
00:32:41,765 --> 00:32:44,535
When I think about how shocked I was earlier...

467
00:32:44,865 --> 00:32:47,065
- Oh, my heart. - I was just...

468
00:32:47,135 --> 00:32:50,005
going to get something CEO Ji needed,

469
00:32:50,065 --> 00:32:52,475
but this woman just grabbed my hair out of nowhere.

470
00:32:52,535 --> 00:32:55,245
But that's no reason to call the police right away.

471
00:32:55,305 --> 00:32:57,515
And to be frank, miss, you didn't just stand there either.

472
00:32:57,575 --> 00:33:00,815
Oh, what a life. What did I do in a past life...

473
00:33:00,885 --> 00:33:02,445
to deserve such humiliation?

474
00:33:02,515 --> 00:33:04,555
This is so unfair, I can't take it. I just can't.

475
00:33:04,615 --> 00:33:06,515
I should just bite my tongue and die. I really should.

476
00:33:06,585 --> 00:33:09,025
Mom, come on. Don't say that.

477
00:33:09,425 --> 00:33:12,625
Hey. Does seeing this mess mean nothing to you?

478
00:33:13,095 --> 00:33:16,295
- Pardon? - If you'd held your rightful place,

479
00:33:16,365 --> 00:33:18,065
do you think any of this would have happened?

480
00:33:18,265 --> 00:33:19,295
It's because you insisted on divorce...

481
00:33:19,365 --> 00:33:21,205
and turned the whole family upside down...

482
00:33:21,335 --> 00:33:24,235
that some crazy woman latched onto our Won Ho!

483
00:33:24,305 --> 00:33:25,535
Mom, that's enough.

484
00:33:25,605 --> 00:33:27,945
Are you having trouble understanding me, ma'am?

485
00:33:28,105 --> 00:33:29,905
CEO Ji's sham of a marriage ended a long time ago.

486
00:33:29,975 --> 00:33:31,275
I already told you that.

487
00:33:31,345 --> 00:33:32,775
I can't believe this crazy tramp.

488
00:33:32,845 --> 00:33:34,345
Will you shut your mouth?

489
00:33:34,445 --> 00:33:35,685
- I'll shut that mouth of yours... - Let go of me.

490
00:33:35,745 --> 00:33:36,745
- Mom. - Mom...

491
00:33:37,115 --> 00:33:38,715
- How dare she! - Mom, let go of her.

492
00:33:38,785 --> 00:33:39,985
- My hair. - Let go!

493
00:33:41,755 --> 00:33:43,585
Calm down!

494
00:33:47,365 --> 00:33:49,065
How did you know the passcode to the house?

495
00:33:51,035 --> 00:33:52,495
Is she really your girlfriend?

496
00:33:54,335 --> 00:33:57,305
- What? - I said she wasn't.

497
00:33:57,605 --> 00:33:59,805
Hey, Won Ho, tell him. She's not, right?

498
00:33:59,975 --> 00:34:03,145
- Well... - I am CEO Ji's girlfriend.

499
00:34:03,205 --> 00:34:05,275
What is with this psycho? Seriously.

500
00:34:05,345 --> 00:34:06,845
Seriously, a joke can only go so far.

501
00:34:06,945 --> 00:34:08,685
Miss, you're going to end up in jail for this.

502
00:34:08,685 --> 00:34:09,715
Hey, Won Ho.

503
00:34:09,785 --> 00:34:10,915
Why are you just standing there, you punk?

504
00:34:10,985 --> 00:34:12,155
Sir, please tell me now,

505
00:34:12,315 --> 00:34:13,655
or should I just charge her with trespassing?

506
00:34:13,715 --> 00:34:17,725
Hurry up. I'm your girlfriend, right?

507
00:34:17,795 --> 00:34:20,795
Hey. Do you think my son is crazy to date a girl like you?

508
00:34:20,865 --> 00:34:22,365
That's right. I am crazy.

509
00:34:23,725 --> 00:34:24,735
Won Ho.

510
00:34:27,635 --> 00:34:28,665
Is that true?

511
00:34:30,135 --> 00:34:31,135
Yes,

512
00:34:31,575 --> 00:34:32,705
I am...

513
00:34:33,305 --> 00:34:34,675
Ahn Hee Ju's...

514
00:34:36,845 --> 00:34:38,215
boyfriend.

515
00:34:50,525 --> 00:34:53,525
Hey, do you believe this? She's his girlfriend?

516
00:34:53,595 --> 00:34:55,195
I'll acknowledge it over my dead body.

517
00:34:55,265 --> 00:34:57,465
That freaking psycho!

518
00:34:58,165 --> 00:34:59,695
Wait, just listen to me before you go.

519
00:35:00,295 --> 00:35:02,965
You have to at least let me explain what happened.

520
00:35:02,965 --> 00:35:04,675
Let go. I don't want to hear it.

521
00:35:04,735 --> 00:35:05,975
Fine, I'll admit it.

522
00:35:05,975 --> 00:35:08,305
Just as you said, Hee Ju isn't just a weird girl.

523
00:35:08,305 --> 00:35:09,505
She's a complete psycho.

524
00:35:09,605 --> 00:35:11,745
But I can't throw her in jail for that.

525
00:35:11,745 --> 00:35:14,245
You saw my mom, didn't you? If I hadn't defended like that...

526
00:35:14,815 --> 00:35:16,185
Did she break down the door?

527
00:35:16,545 --> 00:35:19,455
- What? - You two must be quite serious.

528
00:35:19,515 --> 00:35:22,825
- It's not like that, really. - Let's just end this already.

529
00:35:23,185 --> 00:35:24,795
Mi Young, wait...

530
00:35:29,825 --> 00:35:31,595
Darn it.

531
00:35:41,005 --> 00:35:43,045
(Yeonnam Police Station)

532
00:35:43,305 --> 00:35:44,545
CEO Ji.

533
00:35:46,315 --> 00:35:47,315
Hey!

534
00:35:47,985 --> 00:35:51,085
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

535
00:35:54,025 --> 00:35:55,255
Why you...

536
00:36:05,435 --> 00:36:06,935
You, tell me.

537
00:36:07,365 --> 00:36:09,735
What were you thinking?

538
00:36:11,675 --> 00:36:12,875
I'm sorry.

539
00:36:14,305 --> 00:36:15,945
The other day, by chance,

540
00:36:16,005 --> 00:36:18,575
I happened to see you putting in your passcode,

541
00:36:18,815 --> 00:36:20,075
and out of curiosity...

542
00:36:21,285 --> 00:36:22,515
I must have been crazy.

543
00:36:22,745 --> 00:36:24,455
I was so wrong.

544
00:36:24,515 --> 00:36:26,685
Fine. Let's put that aside.

545
00:36:26,915 --> 00:36:29,055
But what about the girlfriend part?

546
00:36:29,155 --> 00:36:31,195
If I didn't say that,

547
00:36:31,855 --> 00:36:33,595
I was afraid I'd look like a weirdo...

548
00:36:33,655 --> 00:36:37,565
You're already way past weird. You're a complete lunatic. Got it?

549
00:36:42,435 --> 00:36:43,735
Crying isn't going to work.

550
00:36:44,505 --> 00:36:46,005
I'm never seeing you again.

551
00:36:51,275 --> 00:36:53,345
Let go of me while I'm still being nice.

552
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:55,045
Please.

553
00:36:55,445 --> 00:36:56,845
Please, don't be mad.

554
00:36:57,485 --> 00:37:00,055
You're the one who needs to stop. Let's just stop.

555
00:37:01,885 --> 00:37:03,125
Then use me.

556
00:37:06,295 --> 00:37:07,295
What?

557
00:37:07,625 --> 00:37:10,465
I heard you and your wife talking.

558
00:37:10,665 --> 00:37:12,495
You really want to end things now, don't you?

559
00:37:13,735 --> 00:37:15,905
But you're struggling because it isn't working out.

560
00:37:16,305 --> 00:37:19,205
- What does that have to do with... - Since it's come to this anyway...

561
00:37:22,645 --> 00:37:23,975
Just use me.

562
00:37:25,445 --> 00:37:26,815
It's how I can survive,

563
00:37:28,385 --> 00:37:30,045
and it's how you can survive too.

564
00:37:32,785 --> 00:37:34,055
I'll help you.

565
00:37:52,805 --> 00:37:54,545
I spoke with Father Kwon,

566
00:37:55,205 --> 00:37:56,775
and he thinks that for now, instead of a vow renewal,

567
00:37:56,845 --> 00:37:59,445
a wedding for multicultural brides would be a better idea.

568
00:38:00,115 --> 00:38:01,715
The organisation Father Kwon works with...

569
00:38:01,785 --> 00:38:03,445
has a lot more multicultural members,

570
00:38:04,215 --> 00:38:06,715
and creating dresses for various races, nationalities,

571
00:38:06,715 --> 00:38:07,955
and body types...

572
00:38:08,825 --> 00:38:10,955
would be a great experience for us too.

573
00:38:11,895 --> 00:38:13,155
Fine, do that then.

574
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:17,735
Are you really okay with this?

575
00:38:18,165 --> 00:38:19,465
Why are you asking me?

576
00:38:19,465 --> 00:38:21,665
You can discuss that with your girlfriend now.

577
00:38:22,035 --> 00:38:24,105
- What? - Are you done?

578
00:38:24,505 --> 00:38:25,705
I'm leaving now.

579
00:38:27,545 --> 00:38:29,075
I need to ask you for something.

580
00:38:34,685 --> 00:38:36,645
I need you to sign a written pledge.

581
00:38:37,785 --> 00:38:38,785
A written pledge?

582
00:38:39,385 --> 00:38:40,385
Yes.

583
00:38:41,225 --> 00:38:42,625
That even if Hee Ju and I see each other,

584
00:38:42,755 --> 00:38:45,625
you won't raise any objections in the future.

585
00:38:51,965 --> 00:38:53,195
Is that for real?

586
00:38:53,635 --> 00:38:56,765
Well, it's not like I have time to make things up.

587
00:38:56,965 --> 00:38:57,975
My gosh.

588
00:38:59,035 --> 00:39:01,445
- I mean, how could he... - I know.

589
00:39:01,445 --> 00:39:04,445
But seriously, why is CEO Ji acting like this?

590
00:39:04,975 --> 00:39:05,975
I know.

591
00:39:06,815 --> 00:39:07,915
Maybe the stress from the divorce lawsuit...

592
00:39:07,985 --> 00:39:08,985
was too much for him?

593
00:39:09,145 --> 00:39:11,155
The divorce isn't even finalised yet,

594
00:39:11,215 --> 00:39:12,615
but he's already dating...

595
00:39:14,525 --> 00:39:18,255
And CEO Baek, didn't you agree to it too easily?

596
00:39:19,095 --> 00:39:20,595
Without even talking to your lawyer?

597
00:39:20,965 --> 00:39:23,225
He asked so matter-of-factly...

598
00:39:23,295 --> 00:39:25,735
that I didn't even have a chance to think or respond.

599
00:39:25,965 --> 00:39:29,705
Gosh, between CEO Ji demanding something like that...

600
00:39:30,365 --> 00:39:33,305
and CEO Baek just agreeing to it,

601
00:39:34,075 --> 00:39:36,645
you're both really something else.

602
00:39:37,105 --> 00:39:38,115
Unbelievable.

603
00:39:38,545 --> 00:39:43,085
But what is it about that woman that has CEO Ji so captivated?

604
00:39:43,585 --> 00:39:44,585
Is it because she's pretty?

605
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:48,055
Or because she's young?

606
00:39:48,825 --> 00:39:50,895
Oh, honestly.

607
00:39:52,425 --> 00:39:56,125
Anyway, are you really okay, CEO Baek?

608
00:39:56,625 --> 00:39:58,835
Yes. Why wouldn't I be okay?

609
00:39:59,535 --> 00:40:00,695
We're getting a divorce anyway.

610
00:40:03,635 --> 00:40:06,105
Hey, think before you speak.

611
00:40:14,215 --> 00:40:16,585
You did great.

612
00:40:17,245 --> 00:40:19,185
For once, you made a rational decision...

613
00:40:19,185 --> 00:40:20,255
and handled things well.

614
00:40:20,315 --> 00:40:23,825
This is the first time I'm ever going to praise you.

615
00:40:24,125 --> 00:40:26,325
You did great.

616
00:40:28,195 --> 00:40:30,195
Why are you being so formal all of a sudden?

617
00:40:30,365 --> 00:40:32,135
I have to be.

618
00:40:32,535 --> 00:40:33,765
In the middle of a divorce lawsuit,

619
00:40:34,165 --> 00:40:36,835
it's not enough that you're dating someone 12 years younger,

620
00:40:36,965 --> 00:40:38,675
but you even got a written pledge.

621
00:40:39,175 --> 00:40:41,105
As someone who's still single,

622
00:40:41,275 --> 00:40:43,305
you're a legend in my book.

623
00:40:44,645 --> 00:40:46,315
Oh, come on. Stop it.

624
00:40:47,575 --> 00:40:49,615
That written pledge is useless.

625
00:40:51,155 --> 00:40:54,085
- Pardon? - I told you not to play with fire.

626
00:40:54,155 --> 00:40:57,185
And now you're openly dating after getting a written pledge?

627
00:40:57,255 --> 00:40:58,555
Are you out of your mind?

628
00:40:59,025 --> 00:41:00,825
What did your wife even write in that pledge?

629
00:41:01,195 --> 00:41:03,725
That you, her husband, can date another woman,

630
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:04,995
and she won't try to mess up the lawsuit?

631
00:41:05,065 --> 00:41:06,065
Something like that?

632
00:41:06,265 --> 00:41:08,135
Yes, something like that.

633
00:41:08,435 --> 00:41:10,905
I don't know how Mi Soon ended up with a son like you.

634
00:41:12,575 --> 00:41:15,175
So, am I not allowed to date during the divorce lawsuit?

635
00:41:15,245 --> 00:41:16,945
Does that violate my right to the pursuit of happiness?

636
00:41:17,345 --> 00:41:18,345
It does.

637
00:41:18,815 --> 00:41:21,285
By all means, keep pursuing your happiness.

638
00:41:21,545 --> 00:41:22,845
Knock yourself out.

639
00:41:27,185 --> 00:41:28,885
Hey, do we have any soju?

640
00:41:29,825 --> 00:41:31,925
- Should I get you some? - Bring it over.

641
00:41:33,255 --> 00:41:34,255
The big bottle.

642
00:41:42,735 --> 00:41:44,835
It's totally official now.

643
00:41:45,475 --> 00:41:46,475
What?

644
00:41:46,805 --> 00:41:48,945
I got a written pledge from CEO Baek.

645
00:41:49,405 --> 00:41:50,845
A pledge that says even if I date CEO Ji,

646
00:41:51,015 --> 00:41:52,875
she won't cause any trouble.

647
00:41:54,045 --> 00:41:56,045
She wrote what? A written pledge?

648
00:41:56,515 --> 00:41:57,855
I told you before, didn't I?

649
00:41:58,315 --> 00:42:00,185
That you have to fight for love.

650
00:42:00,655 --> 00:42:03,355
So you're here to brag about...

651
00:42:03,985 --> 00:42:05,155
how you won your prize?

652
00:42:05,495 --> 00:42:07,995
Honestly, isn't this great news for you, too?

653
00:42:10,595 --> 00:42:11,595
Great news?

654
00:42:12,895 --> 00:42:13,935
Well, this is awkward.

655
00:42:15,005 --> 00:42:18,905
I'm afraid I have some bad news for you, Hee Ju.

656
00:42:29,185 --> 00:42:32,515
Hey, is what your wife said true?

657
00:42:33,115 --> 00:42:34,115
What?

658
00:42:34,785 --> 00:42:37,425
You and that woman, Ahn Hee Ju...

659
00:42:38,125 --> 00:42:39,295
Oh, that...

660
00:42:39,855 --> 00:42:41,995
- Then, yes. - Are you out of your mind?

661
00:42:42,525 --> 00:42:44,595
How could you do this during the lawsuit?

662
00:42:44,895 --> 00:42:47,695
It just happened that way.

663
00:42:48,305 --> 00:42:50,765
Hey, be honest. There's something else, isn't there?

664
00:42:51,735 --> 00:42:54,335
Is she blackmailing you with something she has on you?

665
00:42:54,975 --> 00:42:56,275
Hey, how did you know?

666
00:42:57,245 --> 00:42:58,245
For real?

667
00:42:58,645 --> 00:43:00,145
Of course not, you idiot. I'm kidding.

668
00:43:01,085 --> 00:43:03,315
Do you really think I'd let some kid intimidate me?

669
00:43:14,865 --> 00:43:15,865
Where are you going?

670
00:43:17,125 --> 00:43:18,235
To see that kid.

671
00:43:42,755 --> 00:43:43,755
What?

672
00:43:44,385 --> 00:43:45,455
Unbelievable.

673
00:43:49,125 --> 00:43:50,225
Vice President Kang?

674
00:43:52,565 --> 00:43:53,965
Manager Song.

675
00:43:54,565 --> 00:43:57,505
Is something wrong?

676
00:43:58,035 --> 00:44:00,835
I'm just fuming.

677
00:44:01,605 --> 00:44:02,605
Fuming?

678
00:44:04,105 --> 00:44:05,115
Manager Song,

679
00:44:05,675 --> 00:44:08,285
do you know anything about Ahn Hee Ju?

680
00:44:09,115 --> 00:44:10,145
Ahn Hee Ju?

681
00:44:13,815 --> 00:44:16,725
CEO Ji's new girlfriend?

682
00:44:16,825 --> 00:44:18,425
Don't give me that "girlfriend" nonsense.

683
00:44:18,795 --> 00:44:21,695
You scared me. Why are you yelling?

684
00:44:24,895 --> 00:44:26,995
Manager Song, don't go around...

685
00:44:27,735 --> 00:44:29,135
saying things like that so carelessly.

686
00:44:29,835 --> 00:44:30,835
What?

687
00:44:35,575 --> 00:44:36,875
Goodness.

688
00:44:40,145 --> 00:44:41,215
What's with him?

689
00:44:49,125 --> 00:44:51,085
Everyone's going to think I'm crazy.

690
00:44:54,295 --> 00:44:56,495
Getting a written pledge during a lawsuit just to date someone.

691
00:44:57,865 --> 00:44:59,035
Especially with someone like you.

692
00:44:59,365 --> 00:45:00,735
What's wrong with someone like me?

693
00:45:02,965 --> 00:45:05,905
Are we sure this is okay to do? Is this the best way?

694
00:45:06,305 --> 00:45:08,205
This way, you can get a clean break.

695
00:45:08,875 --> 00:45:11,845
I'm sure that by now, your wife's feelings...

696
00:45:12,315 --> 00:45:14,075
are plummeting.

697
00:45:14,715 --> 00:45:16,185
Her affection for you is just gone.

698
00:45:17,915 --> 00:45:20,985
By the way, you haven't told anyone...

699
00:45:21,655 --> 00:45:23,425
about us pretending to date, right?

700
00:45:25,055 --> 00:45:26,155
Right.

701
00:45:26,625 --> 00:45:27,655
Okay.

702
00:45:28,525 --> 00:45:30,195
Confidentiality is key for something like this.

703
00:45:30,765 --> 00:45:32,635
You sound like a secret agent.

704
00:45:34,135 --> 00:45:36,735
Oh, right. I got fired.

705
00:45:37,865 --> 00:45:41,675
- What? - I was fired by Calvin.

706
00:45:42,505 --> 00:45:44,645
What? Why? Why'd you suddenly get fired?

707
00:45:45,115 --> 00:45:46,245
I'm not sure.

708
00:45:46,845 --> 00:45:49,815
It's probably either jealousy or revenge.

709
00:45:50,385 --> 00:45:51,385
What are you talking about?

710
00:45:51,615 --> 00:45:53,955
"How dare you get into a relationship before I do?"

711
00:45:54,415 --> 00:45:55,425
That's the jealousy.

712
00:45:56,155 --> 00:45:58,355
"For making my woman uncomfortable."

713
00:45:59,525 --> 00:46:00,525
That's the revenge.

714
00:46:01,095 --> 00:46:04,325
What? "Making my woman uncomfortable"?

715
00:46:04,665 --> 00:46:06,365
Of course she'd be uncomfortable.

716
00:46:06,895 --> 00:46:09,705
The thought of CEO Baek stewing because of me...

717
00:46:10,665 --> 00:46:13,875
is probably enough to tick Calvin off.

718
00:46:18,275 --> 00:46:19,445
CEO Ji.

719
00:46:21,015 --> 00:46:22,915
Can't you help me out?

720
00:46:23,745 --> 00:46:24,755
Help you with what?

721
00:46:24,985 --> 00:46:26,885
Are you just going to leave me like this?

722
00:46:27,755 --> 00:46:30,785
As a victim of Calvin's revenge?

723
00:46:36,665 --> 00:46:37,965
This dish has cilantro in it.

724
00:46:38,335 --> 00:46:40,635
- Yes. - Can I get one without cilantro?

725
00:46:40,965 --> 00:46:41,965
Yes.

726
00:46:45,575 --> 00:46:46,775
Mi Young, you don't eat cilantro.

727
00:46:48,845 --> 00:46:50,245
You remembered.

728
00:46:51,145 --> 00:46:52,515
Here, let's eat.

729
00:46:56,385 --> 00:46:58,415
I heard you fired Hee Ju.

730
00:47:00,585 --> 00:47:05,195
Was it because of me? Because you thought I'd be upset?

731
00:47:05,725 --> 00:47:09,365
No. She deserved to be fired.

732
00:47:10,895 --> 00:47:13,965
If you really did do it because of me,

733
00:47:14,295 --> 00:47:15,405
it was a complete failure.

734
00:47:17,005 --> 00:47:19,875
As of today, Hee Ju is working at our company.

735
00:47:20,475 --> 00:47:23,605
She got fast-tracked thanks to my husband's pull.

736
00:47:29,145 --> 00:47:31,685
Hey, I'm fine. Don't look at me like that.

737
00:47:34,355 --> 00:47:35,355
Mi Young.

738
00:47:41,395 --> 00:47:42,395
This is delicious.

739
00:47:43,125 --> 00:47:44,425
This place is really good.

740
00:47:49,305 --> 00:47:51,065
- Start wrapping up and head inside. - Okay.

741
00:47:51,065 --> 00:47:52,075
All right.

742
00:47:53,735 --> 00:47:54,745
Ji Won Ho.

743
00:48:00,815 --> 00:48:01,885
Darn it.

744
00:48:08,255 --> 00:48:10,755
Seeing you camped out here waiting for me,

745
00:48:11,025 --> 00:48:12,425
you must have a lot of free time these days.

746
00:48:12,855 --> 00:48:15,925
I almost did, but things are getting more complicated.

747
00:48:16,525 --> 00:48:17,525
Because of you.

748
00:48:17,725 --> 00:48:19,835
- What? - I'll get straight to the point.

749
00:48:20,465 --> 00:48:22,965
Fire Ahn Hee Ju.

750
00:48:25,805 --> 00:48:26,805
Why should I?

751
00:48:27,405 --> 00:48:28,905
Why would I do that?

752
00:48:29,305 --> 00:48:33,075
Then why, out of all the photographers,

753
00:48:33,815 --> 00:48:35,385
did you have to hire Ahn Hee Ju?

754
00:48:40,955 --> 00:48:43,955
You didn't think about Mi Young at all, did you?

755
00:48:44,655 --> 00:48:47,725
- What? - When people make decisions,

756
00:48:48,525 --> 00:48:49,725
there's such a thing as common courtesy.

757
00:48:50,925 --> 00:48:53,435
I don't care what you decide to do,

758
00:48:54,195 --> 00:48:57,205
but your lack of courtesy is really rubbing me the wrong way.

759
00:48:58,235 --> 00:48:59,535
So, you showing up unannounced...

760
00:48:59,605 --> 00:49:02,045
and telling me whether or not to fire my employee,

761
00:49:02,675 --> 00:49:03,845
is that what you call courteous?

762
00:49:05,945 --> 00:49:08,785
I'll handle my own employees, so stay out of it.

763
00:49:09,315 --> 00:49:12,755
I find this kind of confrontation extremely unpleasant.

764
00:49:32,175 --> 00:49:34,875
Who was in this room...

765
00:49:41,515 --> 00:49:43,485
When you work hard and win a case,

766
00:49:43,685 --> 00:49:46,355
the payoff is pretty good.

767
00:49:49,285 --> 00:49:50,385
Gosh.

768
00:49:51,055 --> 00:49:52,725
She's surprisingly cute.

769
00:49:53,895 --> 00:49:54,965
Did something good happen?

770
00:49:55,425 --> 00:49:56,425
Gosh, you scared me.

771
00:49:56,895 --> 00:49:57,965
When did you get here?

772
00:50:00,165 --> 00:50:01,505
Got a minute to talk?

773
00:50:11,715 --> 00:50:12,775
It wasn't you.

774
00:50:16,015 --> 00:50:17,015
It was me.

775
00:50:18,815 --> 00:50:20,915
I was the one who put you in danger.

776
00:50:22,555 --> 00:50:23,555
I...

777
00:50:24,425 --> 00:50:26,495
I almost killed you.

778
00:50:28,725 --> 00:50:29,725
Someone might see us.

779
00:50:30,265 --> 00:50:31,265
Get up.

780
00:50:45,145 --> 00:50:46,245
I think my husband...

781
00:50:46,775 --> 00:50:48,515
is dating Hee Ju.

782
00:50:51,215 --> 00:50:54,215
I just went to the motel to get my husband,

783
00:50:55,385 --> 00:50:57,225
and Hee Ju was in the hallway.

784
00:50:59,695 --> 00:51:02,565
He blew up when he saw me,

785
00:51:04,465 --> 00:51:06,135
and I think it must have been because of Hee Ju.

786
00:51:24,185 --> 00:51:27,115
As of today, Hee Ju is working at our company.

787
00:51:27,555 --> 00:51:28,685
Thanks to my husband's pull.

788
00:51:29,025 --> 00:51:31,855
I'll handle my own employees, so stay out of it.

789
00:51:32,355 --> 00:51:35,825
I find this kind of confrontation extremely unpleasant.

790
00:51:38,365 --> 00:51:39,765
I told you before, didn't I?

791
00:51:40,435 --> 00:51:42,365
That you have to fight for love.

792
00:51:52,775 --> 00:51:53,775
What?

793
00:51:54,015 --> 00:51:56,045
Wait, you signed a written pledge about dating that girl?

794
00:51:56,215 --> 00:51:57,715
Are you out of your mind?

795
00:51:57,945 --> 00:52:00,755
Look, I told you. We both agreed to it.

796
00:52:00,815 --> 00:52:02,185
It's not because I actually like her.

797
00:52:02,385 --> 00:52:03,985
That's even weirder, man.

798
00:52:04,185 --> 00:52:06,455
If you genuinely liked the woman,

799
00:52:06,695 --> 00:52:07,955
then I could at least understand.

800
00:52:08,765 --> 00:52:10,425
But with a woman you don't even have feelings for...

801
00:52:12,365 --> 00:52:14,135
Hey, what do you think Mi Young will think?

802
00:52:14,535 --> 00:52:17,005
Well, she'll think I'm crazy.

803
00:52:17,705 --> 00:52:19,635
Dating someone in the middle of all this,

804
00:52:19,705 --> 00:52:20,935
like some woman-crazed lunatic.

805
00:52:21,205 --> 00:52:22,405
And you did it anyway, knowing that?

806
00:52:25,745 --> 00:52:27,245
I'm just going to be the bad guy, Seung Ho.

807
00:52:29,385 --> 00:52:31,415
I need Mi Young to think I'm a complete psycho...

808
00:52:32,315 --> 00:52:34,115
and that I'm someone she never wants to see again.

809
00:52:34,185 --> 00:52:35,685
That's the only way this will really be over.

810
00:52:38,895 --> 00:52:40,055
You're not confident, are you?

811
00:52:42,065 --> 00:52:43,895
The truth is, you're the one who's wavering.

812
00:52:44,525 --> 00:52:45,695
Your heart...

813
00:52:46,395 --> 00:52:48,335
can't let Mi Young go, right?

814
00:52:50,535 --> 00:52:51,535
Hey, Won Ho.

815
00:52:52,435 --> 00:52:55,675
Can't you just talk to Mi Young again and work things out?

816
00:52:57,345 --> 00:52:59,615
I'm saying this because I feel so bad for you.

817
00:52:59,675 --> 00:53:01,845
- Even now, go to Mi Young... - It's too late.

818
00:53:06,055 --> 00:53:07,655
For that to happen, Mi Young and I...

819
00:53:10,385 --> 00:53:11,825
I think we've come too far.

820
00:54:02,175 --> 00:54:03,175
Okay.

821
00:54:05,545 --> 00:54:06,545
Yes.

822
00:54:10,985 --> 00:54:13,385
Have you decided on a location for your wedding photos?

823
00:54:13,855 --> 00:54:16,485
We have a location in mind,

824
00:54:16,555 --> 00:54:18,125
but because of the nature of the location,

825
00:54:18,755 --> 00:54:21,025
it's a little hard finding a photographer.

826
00:54:23,095 --> 00:54:24,765
What's the location?

827
00:54:24,995 --> 00:54:25,995
- A cliff. - It's a cliff.

828
00:54:26,165 --> 00:54:28,095
We met while hiking on a cliff.

829
00:54:28,635 --> 00:54:30,335
And our first kiss also happened to be...

830
00:54:31,005 --> 00:54:32,005
- on the cliff. - On the cliff.

831
00:54:32,305 --> 00:54:33,935
Oh, a cliff.

832
00:54:35,205 --> 00:54:37,405
But if we can't find a photographer who agrees,

833
00:54:37,475 --> 00:54:38,475
we'll just have to scrap the idea.

834
00:54:38,745 --> 00:54:41,115
I hate this, really.

835
00:54:41,245 --> 00:54:42,415
Don't worry, baby.

836
00:54:44,785 --> 00:54:46,055
I'll do it.

837
00:54:57,395 --> 00:54:59,195
That place is too dangerous.

838
00:54:59,495 --> 00:55:02,065
But you have a photographer standing right here,

839
00:55:02,235 --> 00:55:03,235
and you're saying you don't have one?

840
00:55:03,465 --> 00:55:05,975
Hey, they said they want to shoot on a cliff.

841
00:55:06,105 --> 00:55:07,835
I'm telling you right now...

842
00:55:08,105 --> 00:55:10,705
that I'll do the cliff wedding shoot.

843
00:55:11,445 --> 00:55:12,875
Do you not know what a cliff is?

844
00:55:13,115 --> 00:55:15,845
It's a cliff, not some neighbourhood hill.

845
00:55:16,345 --> 00:55:17,845
Does the location really matter?

846
00:55:19,255 --> 00:55:22,325
It doesn't matter. Because I'm a complete professional.

847
00:55:22,585 --> 00:55:24,525
Are you seriously doing this just to prove a point?

848
00:55:24,825 --> 00:55:26,395
Just trust me.

849
00:55:26,955 --> 00:55:29,795
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

850
00:55:36,265 --> 00:55:39,135
There's a place over here with an amazing view of the cliff.

851
00:55:39,205 --> 00:55:41,405
- So beautiful. - Really?

852
00:55:43,205 --> 00:55:44,505
Please follow me carefully.

853
00:55:44,575 --> 00:55:46,015
- Okay. - Careful, darling.

854
00:55:46,015 --> 00:55:47,045
Okay.

855
00:55:47,045 --> 00:55:48,475
Oh, this is so beautiful.

856
00:55:48,985 --> 00:55:52,015
One, two, three. That's lovely.

857
00:55:52,885 --> 00:55:54,585
- Another pose. - Yes.

858
00:55:54,655 --> 00:55:57,425
Okay. One, two, three.

859
00:55:58,385 --> 00:56:01,095
Three. Two, three, and hold.

860
00:56:02,165 --> 00:56:03,165
Just a moment.

861
00:56:10,765 --> 00:56:13,535
- Ready. - Okay, let's keep going. It's fine.

862
00:56:13,605 --> 00:56:14,775
Great.

863
00:56:15,375 --> 00:56:16,375
Are you crazy?

864
00:56:16,805 --> 00:56:19,075
What? A cliff? Not just a mountain, but a cliff?

865
00:56:19,345 --> 00:56:21,915
I didn't force her. Hee Ju volunteered to do it.

866
00:56:21,985 --> 00:56:24,915
She wouldn't have gone if you hadn't brought it up!

867
00:56:25,185 --> 00:56:28,115
I know you're upset with me, but isn't this a bit much?

868
00:56:28,285 --> 00:56:29,755
Is that what you really think?

869
00:56:30,425 --> 00:56:32,495
If you weren't confident, you shouldn't have signed the pledge.

870
00:56:32,755 --> 00:56:33,995
Hey, Ji Won Ho.

871
00:56:35,425 --> 00:56:37,495
Big smiles, please.

872
00:56:38,665 --> 00:56:40,095
You look so beautiful.

873
00:56:40,265 --> 00:56:42,035
Oh, you're the best.

874
00:56:42,935 --> 00:56:44,565
Gorgeous. One more time.

875
00:56:44,905 --> 00:56:46,335
- Okay. - Here we go.

876
00:56:46,405 --> 00:56:47,405
Cheese.

877
00:56:47,835 --> 00:56:48,945
Smile.

878
00:56:52,645 --> 00:56:53,645
What?

879
00:56:56,045 --> 00:56:57,515
We should wrap things up now.

880
00:56:57,815 --> 00:57:00,055
I'll pack up, so you can head out first.

881
00:57:00,115 --> 00:57:01,985
Okay, break time, okay.

882
00:57:02,055 --> 00:57:04,955
Honey, it's so cold.

883
00:57:11,765 --> 00:57:12,765
Gosh...

884
00:57:19,905 --> 00:57:21,235
Hee Ju, are you okay?

885
00:57:21,835 --> 00:57:23,145
What? You're hurt?

886
00:57:24,245 --> 00:57:26,415
Okay, I'm on my way.

887
00:57:41,395 --> 00:57:42,395
Hey! What is this?

888
00:57:42,465 --> 00:57:43,465
What's going on?

889
00:57:43,825 --> 00:57:45,465
Hey, wait, hold on.

890
00:57:45,535 --> 00:57:47,395
Let me go! Help!

891
00:57:56,445 --> 00:57:58,075
The person you are calling is not answering...

892
00:58:18,525 --> 00:58:21,165
- Hey, excuse me! - Be quiet.

893
00:58:21,235 --> 00:58:22,235
- Hey. - Stay still.

894
00:58:22,635 --> 00:58:24,065
- Hey. - Shut your mouth.

895
00:58:24,135 --> 00:58:25,805
- Hey. - Calm down.

896
00:58:26,205 --> 00:58:27,475
Let's go quietly.

897
00:58:45,595 --> 00:58:47,125
- What is this? - Be quiet.

898
00:58:47,195 --> 00:58:49,265
Hey, who are you guys? Why are you doing this...

899
00:58:50,165 --> 00:58:51,265
Hee Ju...

900
00:58:52,395 --> 00:58:53,535
Hee Ju...

901
00:59:00,535 --> 00:59:02,305
Just trust me.

902
00:59:02,875 --> 00:59:05,875
I promise I'll make it back in one piece.

903
00:59:10,015 --> 00:59:11,385
- Stay still. - Hey!

904
00:59:11,445 --> 00:59:13,385
- Hey, you punk. - Darn it.

905
00:59:13,385 --> 00:59:15,525
- Hey, darn it. - Hey, you bastard.

906
00:59:16,455 --> 00:59:17,755
- Hey! - Shut up!

907
00:59:17,825 --> 00:59:18,825
Darn it!

908
00:59:19,095 --> 00:59:21,695
- Let go of me. - Hee Ju!

909
00:59:47,055 --> 00:59:48,455
- I'm not getting out! - Get out.

910
00:59:48,515 --> 00:59:49,785
- I'm not getting out, you bastards. - Get out!

911
00:59:50,525 --> 00:59:51,955
- Hey. - Get over here.

912
00:59:52,055 --> 00:59:53,755
- Come on. - Who are you? Let go of me.

913
00:59:54,325 --> 00:59:56,595
Who are you guys? You've got the wrong person.

914
00:59:58,065 --> 01:00:00,335
Where am I? Who are you people?

915
01:00:00,935 --> 01:00:02,165
Hee Ju!

916
01:00:07,735 --> 01:00:08,735
What?

917
01:00:19,755 --> 01:00:22,425
Hee Ju!

918
01:00:24,555 --> 01:00:28,055
Hee Ju!

919
01:00:38,535 --> 01:00:39,535
What do you think you're doing now?

920
01:00:43,845 --> 01:00:45,575
You... Calvin...

921
01:00:47,115 --> 01:00:48,615
What do you think you're doing?

922
01:00:49,415 --> 01:00:51,085
I didn't want it to come to this.

923
01:00:51,845 --> 01:00:52,855
You haven't forgotten...

924
01:00:53,455 --> 01:00:54,455
the promise, have you?

925
01:00:54,955 --> 01:00:57,255
- Promise? - You remember.

926
01:00:58,555 --> 01:00:59,555
Seven years ago,

927
01:01:00,295 --> 01:01:01,425
the promise we made.

928
01:01:03,665 --> 01:01:04,665
I...

929
01:01:05,065 --> 01:01:06,165
My Mi Young.

930
01:01:06,365 --> 01:01:08,065
Of course I'm going to make her happy.

931
01:01:08,535 --> 01:01:11,865
I will never hurt Mi Young the way you did.

932
01:01:12,935 --> 01:01:15,775
I'll make her so happy that she won't even remember...

933
01:01:15,775 --> 01:01:17,345
her time with you. I'll make sure of it.

934
01:01:23,085 --> 01:01:24,085
Well, then...

935
01:01:25,955 --> 01:01:26,955
Let's go fulfill...

936
01:01:28,315 --> 01:01:29,325
that promise.

937
01:01:51,105 --> 01:01:54,075
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

938
01:01:55,375 --> 01:01:57,215
- It's Calvin. - What?

939
01:01:58,045 --> 01:02:01,785
If I had really wanted to, he would be dead.

940
01:02:02,255 --> 01:02:04,925
Let's just forget about the written pledge too.

941
01:02:04,985 --> 01:02:06,725
Just because of what Calvin said?

942
01:02:08,495 --> 01:02:09,725
CEO Baek,

943
01:02:10,265 --> 01:02:11,695
what is all this?

944
01:02:12,595 --> 01:02:14,195
Seriously, why are you being like this?

945
01:02:14,635 --> 01:02:17,405
It's not like Hee Ju went to that dangerous cliff again.

946
01:02:17,465 --> 01:02:19,335
This could be even more dangerous than the cliff.

947
01:02:19,405 --> 01:02:21,435
- Hey! Hee Ju... - Don't do anything...

948
01:02:21,905 --> 01:02:23,405
for my sake.

